# KFENCE: Kernel Electric-Fence
# Mainline version: 5.12
# Commit: 0ce20dd84089 ("kfence: infrastructure to systematically detect memory safety bugs")
#
# KFENCE is a memory safety error detector for the Linux kernel.
# It uses guard pages to detect out-of-bounds accesses, use-after-free,
# invalid frees, and memory corruption.
#
# Unlike KASAN, KFENCE has near-zero runtime overhead (only ~1 in
# KFENCE_SAMPLE_INTERVAL allocations are guarded), making it suitable
# for production use.
#
# Source files (new):
#   mm/kfence/            — core implementation
#   include/linux/kfence.h — public API
#   arch/arm64/include/asm/kfence.h — arm64 arch support
#   lib/test_kfence.c     — self-tests
#
# Backport notes for 4.19:
#   - Requires SLAB/SLUB allocator hooks (4.19 has different API)
#   - arch/arm64 kfence support needs pgtable handling changes
#   - Documentation files skipped (not needed for compilation)
#   - Some debugfs/locking APIs differ between 4.19 and 5.12
#
# Config options:
#   CONFIG_KFENCE=y
#   CONFIG_KFENCE_SAMPLE_INTERVAL=100
#   CONFIG_KFENCE_NUM_OBJECTS=255
#   CONFIG_KFENCE_STRESS_TEST_FAULTS=0
#
# Risk: Medium-High (allocator API differences)
# Benefit: High (catches memory safety bugs with near-zero overhead)
